\p
\v 1 The¦114266 Israelis¦114261 did \add ≈things that Yahweh¦114264 considered evil¦114262 so\add* \add *he¦114265\add* handed them¦114265 over to the¦114267 Midian¦114269 for seven¦114270 years¦114271
\v 2 and the \add ≈Midianites oppressed\add* \add *them\add* badly. \add ≈It was so bad that¦114290 the Israelis¦114286\add* made¦114282 dens¦114289 for themselves up in the hills¦114291, in caves¦114294, and \add ≈in small, fortified settlements\add*.
\v 3 Whenever the Israelis¦114303 planted a crop, the Midianites or the Amalekites¦114306, or eastern¦114309 groups would¦114304 attack \add #them\add*.
\v 4 They¦114313 would set up their camps around them¦114314 and destroy¦114315 the crops as far away as Gaza¦114323—they¦114326 left¦114326 \add ≈nothing for the Israelis¦114328 to eat\add*, and \add ≡no\add* \add #sheep¦114329, cattle, or donkeys¦114331\add*.
\v 5 It was like a swarm¦114340 of¦114335 locusts¦114342 when they'd \add all\add* come with their tents¦114337 and¦114337 their livestock¦114335—you couldn't even count their camels¦114345! They¦114348 entered the¦114349 region to¦114350 \add ≈totally ravage\add* it¦114350.
\v 6 Thus Yisrael¦114353 was \add ≈severely weakened\add* by Midian¦114356, and¦114357 the¦114358 Israelis¦114360 cried¦114357 out¦114357 to¦114361 Yahweh¦114363.
\p
