\p
\v 4 Then¦115786 Gideon¦115787 and¦115786 his three¦115791 hundred¦115793 warriors crossed the Yordan¦115788 \add going east\add*. They were \add ≈all exhausted¦115797, but¦115786 continued the pursuit¦115798\add*.
\v 5 \add When they arrived at the town\add* of Sukkot¦115802, Gideon asked the \add ≈leaders\add*, “Please¦115805 give¦115803 my men¦115801 some bread¦115807 to eat because¦115811 they're exhausted¦115813, \add ≈but¦115800 we're chasing¦115816\add* Zebah¦115818 and¦115800 Zalmunna¦115819, the Midianite kings¦115820.”
