\p
\v 29 Then \add Gideon\add* (Yoash's¦116265 son¦116263, \add also known as\add* Yerub-Baal) went¦116261 back and lived¦116266 in¦116267 his¦116267 house¦116267,
\v 30 and¦116269 \add *he\add* fathered seventy¦116271 sons¦116272 because¦116275 he had many¦116278 wives¦116277.
\v 31 He¦116293 \add also\add* had a mistress in¦116284 Shekem¦116284—she also bore¦116285 him a son¦116291 that he¦116292 named Abimelek¦116296.
\v 32 Gideon¦116299 died¦116298 at a good¦116304 old¦116303 age¦116303 and¦116305 was¦116305 buried¦116305 in¦116303 the tomb¦116306 of Yoash¦116302 his¦116308 father¦116308, at Ofrah¦116307 of the \add #Abiezerites\add*.
\p
\v 33 \add ≈However\add* after¦116322 Gideon¦116317 had¦116316 died¦116316, the \add ≈Israelis¦116320\add* turned¦116318 away again¦116318 \add from Yahweh\add* and prostituted¦116321 themselves to the Baals¦116323—making¦116324 Baal¦116326-Berit¦116327 for¦116325 themselves as a god¦116328.
\v 34 \add *They¦116333\add* \add ≈forgot about¦116344\add* their god¦116337 Yahweh¦116336—the one who¦116338 had¦116338 rescued¦116338 them¦116339 from¦116340 the \add ≈clutch\add* of all of their enemies¦116343 all around.
\v 35 They¦116353 didn't¦116346 \add ≈show lasting loyalty¦116349\add* to¦116355 Gideon's¦116354 \add ≈family, despite\add* all¦116355 the¦116357 good¦116357 that¦116358 he'd done¦116359 within Yisrael¦116362.
\c 9
