\p
\v 3 After¦117514 him¦117510, Yair¦117511 the¦117512 Gileadite¦117512 \add ≈led\add* Yisrael¦117516 for twenty-two¦117517 years¦117519.
\v 4 He¦117521 had thirty sons¦117525 that¦117542 rode¦117526 on¦117527 thirty donkeys¦117530. There were thirty cities¦117532 for them in the Gilead¦117544 region¦117543 which¦117542 they call¦117535 Yair's¦117538 villages¦117537 to this day¦117540.
\v 5 Then¦117546 Yair¦117547 died¦117546 and¦117548 he¦117548 was¦117548 buried¦117548 in¦117549 Kamon¦117549.
\s1 The making again of bad of Israelis
\rem /s1 Oppression by the Ammonites; The Ammonites Oppress Israel; Jephthah
\p
\v 6 The \add ≈Israelis¦117555\add* continued to do¦117556 \add ≈what Yahweh considered evil¦117557\add*: they¦117560 worshipped the Ba'als, the Ashtorets, the gods of Aram¦117570, the gods of Sidon¦117574, the gods of Moab¦117578, the gods of the sons of Ammon¦117583, and the gods of the Philistines¦117586. They¦117587 forsook Yahweh and didn't¦117591 serve¦117560 him¦117592.
\v 7 Yahweh¦117597 \add ≈was very angry with¦117598\add* Yisrael¦117598, so he¦117599 \add ≈allowed the Philistines¦117602 and¦117594 the Ammonites¦117605 to harass them\add*.
\v 8 They shattered¦117607 and¦117607 oppressed the \add ≈Israelis\add* that¦117629 year¦117613, \add ≈but¦117607 it went on\add* for eighteen¦117615 years¦117617 for all¦117620 the \add ≈Israelis\add* who¦117624 were¦117625 on the opposite side¦117625 of the Yordan¦117626 in the land¦117627 of the Amorites¦117628, which¦117629 is¦117630 in the Gilead¦117630.
\v 9 Then¦117632 the \add ≈Ammonites¦117635\add* also crossed¦117632 over¦117632 the Yordan¦117638 to¦117639 fight¦117639 against Yehudah¦117642, against Benyamin¦117643, and¦117632 against the \add ≈half-tribe\add* of¦117644 Efrayim¦117645.
\p This¦117647 caused incredible distress¦117646 for the¦117633 \add ≈Israelis¦117633\add*
\v 10 \add ≈so\add* \add *they¦117650\add* cried¦117650 out¦117650 to Yahweh¦117655, “We¦117657 have sinned¦117657 against you, because¦117659 we have abandoned¦117660 our¦117663 god¦117663 and¦117650 we have served¦117664 the¦117667 Ba'als.”
\p
