\v 18 Then¦118131 \add #we\add* went through the wilderness¦118132 and turned away from the land of Edom¦118137 and the land of Moab, then¦118131 went \add the long way\add* \add ≈around¦118133 the eastern border\add* of Moab. They¦118148 camped¦118148 on¦118132 the other¦118149 side¦118149 of the Arnon \add river\add*, but¦118131 they¦118153 didn't¦118151 go within Moab's¦118141 borders¦118158, because¦118156 the Arnon was¦118158 the border of Moab.\x + \xo 11:18: \xt Num 21:4.\x*
\v 19 Yisrael¦118162 sent¦118161 messengers¦118163 to¦118164 the Amorite¦118169 King¦118167 Sihon¦118166, the king¦118170 of¦118170 Heshbon¦118171 \add ≈and¦118161 asked\add* him¦118173, ‘Please¦118174, let¦118175 us¦118175 pass¦118175 through your¦118178 land¦118178 as far as \add #our\add* place¦118181.’\x + \xo 11:19-22: \xt Num 21:21-24.\x*
\v 20 But¦118183 \add King\add* Sihon¦118186 didn't¦118183 trust¦118185 Yisrael passing¦118190 through within his border, \add ≈so\add* \add *he\add* assembled all¦118196 of his people¦118198 together and they¦118199 camped at¦118191 Jahaz, and he battled with¦118191 Yisrael.
\v 21 Then¦118206 Yisrael's¦118210 god¦118208, Yahweh¦118207, handed \add King\add* Sihon¦118213 and all his¦118218 people¦118218 over to Yisrael and \add ≈we\add* defeated¦118221 them¦118221. Thus Yisrael took¦118222 possession¦118222 of all of the land¦118227 of the Amorites¦118228 inhabiting that¦118231 region¦118227—
\v 22 everything within the Amorite¦118238 territory¦118237 from the Arnon¦118239 \add river\add* to the Yabbok¦118242, and¦118233 from the wilderness¦118245 as far as the Jordan¦118248.
