\p
\v 1 Now the men¦118621 of Efrayim¦118622 were summoned¦118637 and they passed¦118623 northward¦118624 and they said¦118625 to Yiftah¦118626, “Why¦118627 did¦118629 you pass¦118629 through in¦118632 order to fight¦118631 against¦118632 the \add ≈Ammonites¦118634\add*, but¦118620 you didn't¦118636 call us to go¦118638 with¦118632 you? We're going to burn¦118641 your¦118640 house¦118640 down over¦118642 you!”
\p
\v 2 “\add ≈I've been involved in very intense disputes\add*—my people¦118652 against the \add ≈Ammonites¦118655\add*,” Yiftah¦118646 told them. “When¦118645 I summoned¦118657 you all, you didn't¦118659 \add come and\add* rescue me¦118662 from¦118663 \add ≈them\add*.
\v 3 \add ≈When¦118665\add* I could see¦118665 that¦118688 you weren't coming to assist, I took¦118673 my life¦118674 into my own hands¦118675. I \add ≈advanced against\add* the¦118679 \add ≈Ammonites¦118680\add*, and¦118665 Yahweh¦118682 gave¦118681 \add ≈me victory over\add* them¦118681. \add ≈So¦118665\add* why¦118684 then¦118665 have¦118685 you all come¦118685 \add ≈here\add* to fight¦118689 against me today?”
\v 4 Then¦118692 Yiftah¦118693 assembled all¦118696 of the men of Gilead and¦118692 \add ≈they battled against\add* Efrayim. The¦118705 men of Gilead struck Efrayim because¦118710 they had¦118711 said¦118711, “\add ≈You Gilead people are¦118712 just\add* fugitives¦118712 from Efrayim—\add living here\add* in the middle of Efrayim, in the middle of Menashsheh¦118719.”
\v 5 The Gileadites captured¦118721 the crossing places of the Jordan along Efrayim. Then¦118721 when any of the survivors from Efrayim would say, “May I cross¦118733 over¦118733,” the men¦118736 of Gilead¦118722 would \add ≈ask\add*, “Are you¦118740 an Efrayimite?” If he¦118741 said¦118741, “No¦118743,”
\v 6 then¦118745 they'd \add ≈demand\add*, “\add ≈Now¦118758\add* say¦118747: Shibboleth¦118750.” But¦118745 if he said¦118751 “Sibboleth¦118752” because he \add ≈didn't¦118753 have time to think\add* to pronounce¦118755 it correctly, they would seize¦118757 him and¦118745 would slaughter¦118759 him at those crossing places of¦118762 the¦118763 Yordan¦118763. Forty-two thousand¦118770 from Efrayim¦118767 fell¦118764 at that time.
