\v 14 \add ≈So¦120442\add* \add she did it and\add* fastened¦120442 it with¦120443 the pin, and \add ≈called out\add*, “The Philistines¦120446 are \add ≈here to get\add* you¦120447, Shimshon¦120448!” Then¦120442 he¦120449 woke up and \add ≈ripped\add* out the pin, the loom¦120455, and \add his hair from\add* the fabric.
\p
\v 15 Then¦120460 she¦120460 said¦120460 to him¦120461, “How¦120462 can you say¦120463, ‘I¦120464 love¦120464 you,’ when your heart¦120465 isn't¦120466 with¦120472 me? You've \add ≈been deceitful¦120471 to\add* me three¦120469 times¦120470 \add now\add*, and¦120460 you haven't revealed to me \add ≈the secret of¦120478 your amazing\add* strength¦120478.”
\v 16 \add ≈Day after day¦120489 she nagged and¦120481 pestered¦120490 him¦120490 until he¦120481 was¦120481 sick to death¦120493 of hearing it¦120491\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈So¦120495\add* \add finally\add* he¦120495 told¦120495 her¦120497 \add ≈his¦120502 secret\add*, “\add ≈My hair has¦120508 never been cut\add* because¦120512 I've been a Nazirite¦120514 to¦120504 God¦120515 \add ≈since my birth\add*. If \add ≈my head¦120511\add* would be shaved¦120521, then¦120495 my strength¦120524 would leave¦120522 me, and¦120495 I'd become¦120525 weak—I'd be just like¦120527 any other \add #man\add*.”
\p
\v 18 When¦120531 Delilah¦120532 perceived that¦120535 he'd told her¦120538 \add ≈his deepest secret\add*, she¦120544 summoned the Philistine leaders, “Come¦120549 \add ≈here\add* one more time¦120550, because¦120535 he's¦120553 told me¦120554 \add ≈his secret\add*.” \add ≈So¦120531\add* the Philistine leaders came¦120561, bringing¦120565 the silver¦120566 \add coins\add* \add ≈with¦120567 them\add*.
\v 19 Then¦120576 she made¦120569 him fall asleep¦120569 on¦120570 her¦120572 knees¦120572, and she called¦120573 in a man¦120574 to shave¦120575 off¦120575 his seven¦120578 locks \add ≈of hair\add*, causing him to start to weaken, and his \add additional\add* strength¦120584 left him.
\v 20 Then¦120587 she¦120587 said¦120587, “The¦120588 Philistines¦120588 are¦120589 \add ≈here to get\add* you¦120589, Shimshon¦120590!” He woke up and \add ≈thought to himself\add*, “I'll escape like \add ≈all the other times¦120595\add* and I'll shake¦120597 myself¦120597 loose.” But¦120587 he didn't¦120599 know¦120600 that¦120601 Yahweh¦120602 had¦120603 left him¦120604.
\v 21 \add ≈So¦120606\add* the Philistines¦120607 seized¦120606 him, and they gouged¦120608 out¦120608 his¦120611 eyes¦120611. They¦120612 brought¦120612 him to Gaza¦120614 and chained him with¦120616 a pair of bronze¦120616 shackles¦120616, then¦120606 \add ≈they put him to work in¦120616 prison¦120620\add* grinding¦120618 \add grain\add*.
\v 22 \add ≈However,\add* \add over time\add* his¦120626 hair¦120624 began¦120623 to¦120627 grow¦120627 back¦120627 again.
\s1 Shimshon's death
