\p
\v 23 \add Some time later,\add* the Philistine leaders¦120632 gathered¦120634 together for a celebration and to offer¦120636 a large¦120639 sacrifice¦120637 to their¦120641 god Dagon¦120640, saying¦120643, “Our god has¦120644 \add ≈helped us capture\add* our terrible enemy¦120649, Shimshon¦120648.”
\v 24 When¦120651 the people¦120653 saw¦120651 him, they¦120654 praised¦120654 their¦120657 god, saying¦120659, “Our¦120673 god has¦120660 \add ≈helped us capture\add* our enemy¦120665—the devastator of our region¦120668 who \add ≈killed¦120673 so many of us\add*.”
\v 25 \add ≈Later in the celebration when the drink had liberated their¦120692 thinking\add*, they said¦120680, “Call for¦120685 Shimshon so¦120683 he¦120683 can \add ≈entertain¦120683 us¦120685\add*.” So¦120675 they \add ≈brought\add* Shimshon in from¦120688 the \add ≈prison¦120689\add* and¦120675 \add taunted him\add* \add ≈to¦120687 get them¦120692 all laughing\add*. They¦120693 made¦120693 him stand¦120693 among the pillars¦120696 \add of the building\add*
