\v 27 The¦120719 building was¦120720 full¦120720 of the men and the women, \add ≈including¦120722\add* the Philistine leaders¦120725. On the roof¦120729 there¦120723 were about¦120730 three¦120730 thousand¦120731 men and women watching¦120734 the entertainment with¦120735 Shimshon¦120736.
\p
\v 28 Then¦120738 Shimshon¦120739 called¦120738 out to Yahweh, “My¦120744 master¦120744 Yahweh, please remember¦120746 me. Strengthen¦120748 me please, just this time¦120751, oh God¦120753, so¦120754 that¦120752 I¦120754 can avenge¦120754 myself¦120754 by one \add last\add* act of vengeance¦120755 on the Philistines¦120760 \add to make them pay for\add* my two¦120758 eyes¦120759.”
\v 29 Then¦120762 \add *he¦120762\add* took hold of the two¦120766 centre pillars¦120768 on¦120777 which¦120770 the building depended, and \add ≈pressed out\add* against¦120775 them—one in his right¦120777 hand¦120777 and one in his left¦120779.
\v 30 Then¦120781 \add *he\add* \add ≈exclaimed\add*, “\add ≈Let¦120783 me\add* die¦120783 with the Philistines¦120787!” He¦120782 stretched¦120788 out¦120788 with his strength¦120789 and the building fell¦120790 on¦120789 \add &their\add* leaders¦120794 and all¦120797 of¦120797 the people in¦120789 it¦120802. \add ≈So¦120781\add* he killed more people at¦120789 his death¦120807 than¦120809 he had¦120810 killed during his life¦120811.
\p
\v 31 Then¦120813 his brothers¦120814 and all¦120815 his father's¦120818 household¦120817 went¦120813 \add to Gaza\add* and carried¦120819 \add @his body\add* back. They buried¦120823 him¦120824 between¦120825 Zorah¦120826 and Eshtaol¦120828 in¦120829 the¦120829 burial place of¦120829 his father Manoah¦120830. He had¦120833 \add ≈helped\add* Yisrael¦120836 for twenty¦120837 years¦120838.
\c 17
