\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* there was¦120841 a man¦120843 named Micah¦120848 from¦120844 the hill¦120844 country of¦120846 Ephraim¦120846
\v 2 who \add ≈admitted\add* to¦120851 his¦120851 mother¦120851, “Those \add ≈eleven\add* hundred¦120853 silver¦120854 coins that¦120855 were taken¦120856 from you—\add ≈when you made\add* a curse¦120861, and¦120850 \add ≈even said¦120863 it when I was listening\add*, \add well\add* listen, \add ≈I've got it all\add*—I took¦120870 it myself.”
\p His¦120872 mother said, “May Yahweh¦120875 bless¦120873 you, my¦120874 son¦120874.”
\v 3 Then¦120877 he¦120877 brought¦120877 back¦120877 the \add ≈eleven\add* hundred¦120882 silver¦120883 coins to his mother¦120886 and \add *she¦120885\add* \add ≈declared\add*, “I¦120888 will¦120899 certainly consecrate the money to Yahweh¦120892 \add ≈for my son's¦120894 benefit\add*. \add ≈Take¦120899 it and we'll use it to have one statue carved¦120896 and another cast\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦120902 after the¦120905 money had been returned¦120902,\add* his mother¦120908 gave¦120911 two¦120909 hundred¦120909 silver¦120910 coins to¦120912 a silversmith¦120912. He¦120913 made¦120913 a carved¦120914 figure and one cast \add from a mould\add*, and \add they were placed\add* in¦120917 Micah's¦120918 house¦120917.
