\v 5 Now¦120929 that Micah¦120921 had a \add ≈shrine with gods in it¦120922\add*, he¦120925 made¦120925 \add ≈some priestly robes\add* and \add ≈some household¦120923 gods\add*, and consecrated one of his sons¦120933 as his priest¦120937.
\v 6 In those¦120940 days¦120939, Yisrael¦120943 didn't¦120941 have a king¦120942—each \add ≈person\add* would do¦120947 whatever \add ≈seemed right¦120945 to them\add*.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈Now\add* there¦120963 was¦120950 a young¦120952 Levite¦120959 man¦120952 from the¦120956 family of¦120956 Yehudah\f + \fr 17:7 \ft Maybe one parent was from the tribe of Levi and one from Yehudah?\f* who'd been staying in Bethlehem (in Yehudah).
\v 8 \add *He¦120965\add* left Bethlehem to find¦120973 another place to say, and¦120965 on¦120972 his way, he \add ≈ended up arriving\add* at¦120972 Micah's¦120981 place in¦120972 the Efrayimite hill¦120975 country¦120975.
