\p
\v 1 In those¦121076 days¦121070, Yisrael¦121074 \add ≈didn't¦121072 have¦121087 a\add* king¦121073. The¦121077 tribe¦121077 of¦121077 Dan was¦121079 looking¦121079 for¦121079 land to settle in¦121074, because¦121084 up \add ≈until¦121089 then\add*, \add ≈they hadn't been able to claim their allocated region\add* among the Israeli¦121095 tribes¦121095.
\v 2 \add ≈So\add* the Danites sent¦121100 out five¦121106 capable men (from Zorah¦121113 and from Eshtaol¦121114) to scout out the region and explore it¦121119. They had told them¦121121, “Go¦121122 \add and\add* explore the area.” They came¦121127 to the Efrayimite hill¦121128 country¦121128, as far as Micah's¦121134 house¦121133, and spent¦121135 the night¦121135 there¦121136.
