\v 6 “\add ≈Continue on¦121206\add* in¦121206 peace¦121199,” the¦121197 priest¦121197 said¦121195. “Yahweh¦121201 has \add ≈prepared everything ahead\add* of you all.”
\p
\v 7 Then the five¦121210 men¦121211 left and \add ≈went¦121212 on¦121220\add* to¦121213 Layish¦121213. They saw¦121214 that¦121218 the people¦121217 \add ≈there\add* were living¦121221 in confidence \add ≈just like\add* the Tsidonians were—\add ≈peacefully¦121226\add* and \add feeling\add* secure¦121223. No one¦121231 in the region was causing \add ≈trouble\add* for them and \add ≈they were very settled\add*. They were far away from¦121238 the Tsidonians and \add ≈didn't¦121240 interact with¦121220 others\add*.
\v 8 Then¦121247 they¦121247 went¦121247 \add back\add* to¦121248 their¦121250 relatives in Tsorah¦121251 and¦121247 Eshtaol¦121252, who \add ≈asked\add* them¦121254, “How \add ≈did it go\add*?”
\v 9 “Get¦121268 \add ≈ready immediately\add*,” they¦121259 \add ≈said¦121259\add*, “so that we can go \add to battle\add* against¦121262 them¦121262! Because¦121263 we've¦121264 seen¦121264 the land and¦121259 listen, it's¦121269 incredible good¦121269. \add ≈Don't¦121273 just still there\add*—you all \add ≈need to take action\add* to go in to \add ≈take possession¦121278 of¦121278\add* the land.
\p
\v 10 When you go¦121283, you'll all come¦121284 to a people¦121288 living \add ≈without suspicion of attack\add*, and¦121290 the land is spacious in¦121297 \add ≈all directions\add*, because¦121293 God¦121296 \add ≈will¦121284 hand¦121297 it¦121295 over to you\add*—a place¦121298 where¦121299 there's¦121300 no lack¦121303 of anything that's on¦121297 the earth¦121308.”
\p
\v 11 So¦121310 six¦121316 hundred¦121318 Danite¦121313 \add ≈warriors\add* left¦121310 Tsorah¦121314 and¦121315 Eshtaol¦121315, carrying their weapons¦121321.
\v 12 They \add ≈set off\add* and¦121325 camped at¦121326 Kiriat-Yearim in¦121326 Yehudah¦121328. \add ≈That's why\add* they¦121332 call¦121332 that¦121340 place¦121333 Mahaneh¦121335-Dan \add (meaning ‘Dan's camp’)\add* to this¦121340 day¦121339—it's back behind¦121342 Kiriat-Yearim.
\v 13 From¦121347 there¦121347, they¦121351 crossed over into the Efrayimite¦121350 hill¦121348 country¦121348, \add eventually\add* \add ≈arriving near\add* Micah's¦121355 house¦121354.
\p
\v 14 Then¦121357 the five¦121358 men¦121359 who¦121360 had¦121360 \add ≈been here previously\add* scouting out¦121361 the land¦121364 said¦121366 to¦121367 their¦121369 \add ≈group\add*, “Do¦121365 you know¦121370 that¦121371 there's¦121372 \add ≈a house¦121373 here\add* with¦121373 a \add ≈gear for priests\add*, family idols, a carved¦121377 image, and¦121357 a cast image? So¦121357 now¦121379, consider¦121380 what¦121381 you should do¦121383.”
\v 15 So¦121385 they turned¦121385 \add ≈off the main path\add* and they came¦121387 to¦121388 the place with the young¦121392 Levite¦121393 man¦121392 in Micah's¦121395 house¦121394, and they asked¦121396 about¦121390 his welfare¦121399.
\v 16 The six¦121401 hundred¦121403 Danite men¦121404 stayed outside at the gate¦121410, holding their¦121407 weapons¦121406.
\p
\v 17 The five¦121417 men who'd gone¦121419 to¦121420 scout out¦121420 the land¦121423 went¦121424 in \add around the back\add*. They took¦121426 the carved¦121429 image, the priest's gear, the family idols, and¦121416 the cast image, while the priest was¦121440 standing¦121440 at the entrance¦121441 of¦121441 the gate¦121442 along with the six¦121443 hundred¦121445 armed¦121447 men.
