\c 19
\s1 The Levite and his slave-wife
\rem /s1 The Levite and His Concubine; A Levite and His Concubine; The Levite's Concubine
\p
\v 1 In those¦121762 days¦121761 when there was no king¦121763 over Yisrael¦121765, there was a Levite¦121769 man¦121768 who was staying in the remotest¦121771 parts¦121771 of the hill¦121772 country¦121772 of Efrayim¦121774. He¦121775 took¦121775 a slave-wife for himself from¦121780 Bethlehem in Yehudah¦121782.
\v 2 \add ≈However\add*, \add *she\add* started sleeping around, and then¦121784 she left him¦121788 and went¦121787 to her¦121792 father's¦121792 house¦121791 in Bethlehem \add where she ended up\add* staying for four¦121802 months¦121803.
\v 3 Then¦121805 her husband \add ≈got organised\add* and went¦121807 after¦121808 her—to \add ≈sweet-talk\add* her and persuade her to return with¦121816 him. He took a young¦121824 \add servant\add* man and a team of¦121817 donkeys¦121818. She invited \add @her husband\add* into her father's¦121821 house¦121820, and when \add *her\add* father saw¦121822 him, he¦121825 was glad to meet¦121826 him.
\v 4 His¦121831 father-in-law¦121831 (her father) insisted \add ≈on offering hospitality\add*, so they¦121838 ate¦121838 and drank¦121839, and he stayed the¦121840 night¦121840, and \add ended up\add* staying for three¦121836 days¦121837.
\v 5 Then¦121843 on¦121847 the fourth¦121845 day¦121844, they got up¦121848 early¦121846 and¦121843 \add @the Levite\add* prepared to leave, but¦121843 his¦121855 father-in-law¦121851 \add ≈urged him to eat before they left\add*.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦121864\add* the two of¦121866 them¦121866 ate¦121865 and drank¦121868 together¦121867, and then¦121864 the woman's¦121871 father¦121870 said¦121869, “Please¦121877 stay \add another\add* night¦121878. \add ≈Relax and have a good¦121879 time\add*.”
